      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The theory of defect-mediated two-dimensional melting and the hexatic phase reshaped understanding of phase transitions, order, and topological defects.",
        "attribution": "Young, Halperin, and Nelson are appropriately associated with the theoretical framework that established this account of melting.",
        "maturity": "The theory is longstanding and has received substantial experimental support in two-dimensional systems.",
